      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re-reading this a week later, I think the \"check in the one line shell script\" is still a sound advice; it requires one extra file but I guess it\u0027s better than this exercise in quoting and you may even be able to get away with a static rule:\n\nvar (\n  copyGolden \u003d pctx.AndroidStaticRule(\n    \"copyGolden\", blueprint.RuleParams{\n      Command: \"build/make/scripts/copy_stuff.sh ${in} ${golden}\n  )  \n)\n\nthen\n\nctx.Build(BuildParams{\n  Rule: copyGolden, \n  Inputs: \u003coutput file\u003e,\n  Args: map[string]string{ \"golden\": \u003cgolden file\u003e}})\n  \nOr if that doesn\u0027t work for some reason, at least extract the shell stanza in linees 735-738 into a static rule so that it\u0027s a bit more readable.",
